<section class="not-content">
  <h2>Mobius improves itself</h2>
  <p>Mobius uses its own agents to repair and to extend itself. Each row shows one part of this work.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <p><strong>It repairs itself.</strong> When the CI run of a pull request fails, the Diagnoser reads the job logs and finds the cause. A fix round repairs the pull request. A failure that more than one pull request shows becomes a repair issue of the maintenance Workstream. A break of <code>main</code> becomes a repair issue too. The global switch Repairs starts these tasks.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <p><strong>It writes its own skills.</strong> The Curator reads the sessions of the agents and keeps the memory files of each repository. It proposes a skill from the commands that agents repeat. The Skills Workstream turns each proposal into a pull request. Each new session gets the skills.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <p><strong>Mobius builds Mobius.</strong> Agents of Mobius write the code of Mobius. Most of the merged pull requests in the numbers above are pull requests of Mobius itself.</p>
  </div>
</section>

